// 2D flat-plate cascade (Otsuka et al. 1996 baseline): beta = 15 deg, pitch d = 0.05 m, chord 3d.
// Blade-aligned coordinates: inflow at incidence alphaDeg to the blades (upward -> lower boundary
// bladeSS is the suction side). v5: sigma imposed directly at the INLET (static p_rgh ramp sigmaStart -> sigma) together with the
// fixed inlet velocity; outlet zeroGradient U and p. Outlet-pressure control (v1, v4) runs away to a
// choked supercavity (cavity growth lowers inlet p -> more growth); v2 (p inlet + flowRate outlet)
// diverged numerically; v3 closed-loop controller oscillated once a cavity formed.
// Set sigma / alphaDeg with sed (never foamDictionary -set: it freezes the #eval values).
Uinf        10;
alphaDeg    5.0;
rhoL        999.19;
pSat        3169;
sigma       0.2;
sigmaStart  10.0;
tHold       0.03;
tRamp       0.08;
qInf        #eval{ 0.5*$rhoL*$Uinf*$Uinf };
pIn         #eval{ $pSat + $sigma*$qInf };
pStart      #eval{ $pSat + $sigmaStart*$qInf };
Ux          #eval{ $Uinf*cos(degToRad($alphaDeg)) };
Uy          #eval{ $Uinf*sin(degToRad($alphaDeg)) };
kIn         0.06;
omegaIn     64;
